WEBVTT

00:03:25.993 --> 00:03:30.498
And that really gave me the opportunity
to talk about, you know,

00:03:30.498 --> 00:03:33.209
some of the intersections
of climate change, for example,

00:03:33.209 --> 00:03:34.710
with racial justice.

00:03:35.086 --> 00:03:39.757
MR: Talk about this big long word
that we use, intersectionality.

00:03:39.799 --> 00:03:41.133
(Laughter)

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:44.845
VN: Yeah, so when when we talk
about intersectionality,

00:03:44.887 --> 00:03:46.931
it's just something that explains

00:03:46.931 --> 00:03:49.350
that climate change
is not just on its own.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.102
Climate change is more than weather,

00:03:51.143 --> 00:03:52.478
it's more than statistics,

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:53.813
it's about the people.

00:03:53.854 --> 00:03:57.233
And when we bring in
the conversation of intersectionality,

00:03:57.275 --> 00:04:00.987
it makes us talk about, you know,
things like poverty eradication.